<title>SWEDEN: Assidoman says Q1 profit falls 56 pct.</title>
<headline>Assidoman says Q1 profit falls 56 pct.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-05-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish forestry group AssiDoman posted these earnings for the first quarter of 1997, ending on March 31.</p>
<p>					(million crowns unless stated)</p>
<p> Profit after fin items		  360   vs   827</p>
<p> Sales				     4,816   vs 5,007</p>
<p> Earnings per share (crowns)	  2.20   vs 5.20</p>
<p> Other operating income		   90   vs   416</p>
<p> Operating costs			 4,134   vs 4,282</p>
<p> Depreciation				346   vs   283</p>
<p> Associated interest	    CHARGE   2   vs     5  CREDIT</p>
<p> Operating profit after deprec	 424   vs   863</p>
<p> Net financial items	     CHARGE 64   vs    36 CHARGE</p>
<p> Taxes					 100   vs   214</p>
<p> Net profit				  260   vs   613</p>
<p>NOTE -- Analysts in a Reuter poll expected a profit of 427 million crowns after financial items.</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1017</p>
</text>
